messages:
lia: Quick ping 3 onboarding tickets where users copy quickstart and get "named export not found" or "Cannot read property 'InferenceClient' of undefined".
omar: That's the classic CJS vs ESM mismatch. Which quickstart snippet did they use?
lia: The one with `require('@redwood/inference')` in the README. Some of them are on Node with "type": "module" or on Vercel edge.
rachel: Short-term fix: add a clear, tiny cheatsheet in README with exact copy/paste for four cases (CJS, ESM default, ESM named, TS). People want one-liners.
omar: Agreed. Proposed snippets:
```
// CommonJS (package.json WITHOUT "type": "module")
const Redwood = require('@redwood/inference');
const client = new (Redwood.InferenceClient || Redwood.default?.InferenceClient)({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });

// ESM default (node with "type": "module")
import Redwood from '@redwood/inference';
const client = new Redwood.InferenceClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });

// ESM named (edge runtimes / strict ESM)
import { InferenceClient } from '@redwood/inference';
const client2 = new InferenceClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });
```
lia: Also add a tiny TS hint: `{"compilerOptions": {"esModuleInterop": true, "allowSyntheticDefaultImports": true}}` so .ts examples compile for most users.
lia: We should call out: Edge runtimes (Vercel/Cloudflare) are ESM-only -> use the named/ESM example.
build-bot: Draft docs PR opened: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/559 (adds "JS SDK: CJS/ESM/TS/Edge" section and links to examples).
omar: Operational follow-up: INF-342 to normalize publish outputs (dist/cjs + dist/esm + .d.ts) and add an exports map in package.json. We'll add CI smoke tests that run each example.
rachel: I'll scaffold examples/js/{cjs,esm,ts,edge} and include exact npm/node commands. Also add a tiny troubleshooting step for support: `node -e "console.log(require('@redwood/inference'))"` and `node -p "import('@redwood/inference')"` to inspect how the package resolves.
lia: Good. For now docs + examples should cut tickets. Once PR lands I'll update onboarding checklist and support playbook. Closing thread.
